### Anything else?

The check has behaved this way since it was added in #64069. The [NG8021 docs page](https://angular.dev/extended-diagnostics/NG8021) only shows `prefetch when` next to an implicit `idle` main trigger, never next to a `when` main trigger.

`ngtsc` now refers to constructor injection tokens and host directives through the imports the author wrote (named, aliased, default and `ns.X`) instead of generated `import * as iN` imports. It also elides imports that are only referenced from the Angular decorators it removes, or from the `emitDecoratorMetadata` types of the declarations those decorate.

This matches the output of `ngp`, which is updated to reuse `ns.X` as well. Local compilation, `.d.ts` output and type-only imports are unchanged.

```ts
import {Component, QueryList, ViewChildren} from '@angular/core';
import {Tabs} from './tabs';
import {Dep} from './dep';

@Component({selector: 'my-cmp', template: '', hostDirectives: [Tabs]})
export class MyCmp {
  @ViewChildren('x') items!: QueryList<unknown>;
  constructor(readonly dep: Dep) {}
}
```

Before (abridged):

```js
import { Component, QueryList, ViewChildren } from '@angular/core'; // `QueryList` kept under `emitDecoratorMetadata`
import * as i0 from "@angular/core";
import * as i1 from "./dep";
import * as i2 from "./tabs";
// i0.ɵɵdirectiveInject(i1.Dep)
// i0.ɵɵHostDirectivesFeature([i2.Tabs])
```

After (abridged):

```js
import { Component, ViewChildren } from '@angular/core';
import { Tabs } from './tabs';
import { Dep } from './dep';
import * as i0 from "@angular/core";
// i0.ɵɵdirectiveInject(Dep)
